{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Bo to Pharaoh… bringing tomorrow.</b> And how did Moshe know, for we do not find that the Holy One, blessed be He, told him about the plague of locusts? One may say that they were engraved on the staff — דצ\"ך עד\"ש באח\"ב — and קושיא ל\"ק, if so, for the later plagues why did He need to inform him? Therefore it seems to me that Moshe understood the plague from the fact that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moshe: ״ולמען תספר״, and it is the way to tell about the plague of locusts, for also regarding the plague of locusts of Yoel it is written about it: ״עליה לבניכם ספרו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "דצ\"ך עד\"ש באח\"ב is a standard acronym for the ten plagues; left untranslated as it appears in the original. קושיא ל\"ק read as 'the question does not stand' (i.e., there is no difficulty)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:56.792687438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}